ProgramControl Testing
------------------------
Cases:
Case 1:
Call listFiles() when data files are available
Expected:
Returns the file names

Case 2:
Call listFiles() when no files are there
Excepted:
Returns an empty list<string>

Case 3:
Call getFileContents() with valid number from file list and null for keyFileName
Expected:
Reads the data file, passes default cipher to Cipher, returns the output from Cipher to UserInterface

Case 4:
Call getFileContents() with valid number from the file list and valid (non-null) cipher.
Expected:
Reads the data file, passes file and cipher to Cipher, returns the output to UserInterface

Case 5:
Call getFileContents() with invalid (0 or negative) file number
Expected:
Throws a TopSecretException and doesn't attempt to read file

Case 6:
Call getFileContents() with an invalid (greater than number of files) file number
Expected:
Throws a TopSecretException and doesn't attempt to read file

Case 7:
Call getFileContents with a valid file but invalid cipher
Expected:
Throws an exception and doesn't pass the cipher to Cipher

Case 8:
Call getFileContents with a valid file number which links to an invalid File
Expected:
Throws a TopSecretException and doesn't pass to Cipher